    "causalModel": {
      "founding": "A village grown where nine root-joined trunks stand in one ring; one tree by the Hist's reckoning, nine by the tribes' reckoning.",
      "siteAdvantages": "The ring encloses firm ground and makes its own stockade. The knoll stands 4.8 m above the water table on firm lowland, with poleable water 32 m west and the Archon-Gideon road 160 m south-west.",
      "occupantsMotive": "A tribe that hosts the convocation's overflow and has grown rich on it, renting pitch-rights to delegations that cannot fit at the Tsoko camp.",
      "pressures": "Hosting a province's delegations one month a year has made them arrogant the other eleven. Two neighbouring tribes now camp at Greenspring instead, on principle.",
      "wouldChangeIf": "A convocation held elsewhere would halve the village. The falling attendance the Root Talk ground counts publicly is already showing in their rents."
    },
