          ],
          "chosen": true,
          "why": "A firm-lowland knoll 149 m from the plot: 4.77 m above the water table, ground slope 2.6 deg, and 2.17 m of relief across the whole 66 m ring, so eight of the nine trunks sit on a plinth or a pad and only the elder trunk needs a dug-in flare. Poleable water 32 m west with the shoreline 40 m off, so the ring encloses firm ground rather than standing in it; the Archon-Gideon road passes 160 m south-west, which is the catalogue's road discovery; flood band 0 and no wet-season inundation."
        },
